00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:59.760
within four days of joining the program for Model 3 and Model Y. The rapid uptake shows strong

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:05.060
demand for the vehicles under the incentive. The program covers qualifying purchases through

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:10.760
participating manufacturers. No extension of the current funding round was mentioned. The quick

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:16.540
exhaustion occurred after Tesla added the models to the rebate eligible list. When California's

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:22.320
EV incentive pool vanished in four days after Tesla joined, the speed showed pent-up interest once

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:28.380
the net cost dropped for Model 3 and Model Y buyers. The same pattern appears whenever incentives

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:34.460
appear or disappear. Orders accelerate then settle at a lower baseline once the subsidy ends.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:40.180
Manufacturers that rely on sustained incentives face margin pressure when those supports shrink.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:45.760
While those with stronger brand pull or lower production costs can maintain volume at higher net

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:51.580
prices, that pattern forces a distinction between structural demand and policy-driven demand.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:58.220
Tesla's vehicles compete on range, software, and charging access. Yet the rebate exhaustion data

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:02.940
suggests a meaningful slice of recent volume would not have closed without the extra discount.

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:08.680
The rapid clearance of funds indicates the current lineup retains strong appeal at the subsidized

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:13.940
price point, but the next test will be whether order rates hold once buyers face the full sticker

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:19.140
again. Over time, the industry learns which products still sell when the subsidy is removed,

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:23.960
and that outcome will shape how much of the company's growth can be attributed to product strength

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:30.440
versus temporary policy support. Policy-driven volume also affects planning for battery supply

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:36.400
and factory utilization. When incentives pull forward purchases, production schedules tighten,

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:42.560
and then ease, creating uneven utilization curves that raise per unit costs during lulls.

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:48.640
Tesla's ability to absorb those swings depends on how quickly it can reallocate cells between vehicle

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:54.780
and energy products, or adjust output at gigatexas and Nevada. The California data point

00:04:54.780 --> 00:05:00.840
therefore serves as an early signal of how durable demand remains once external price supports fade,

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:06.400
directly influencing margin forecasts and capital allocation decisions for the balance of the

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:13.060
year. Tesla shares remain nearly 30% below their peak while trading at 330 times earnings.

